@@ -30,18 +30,23 @@ known categories stays in the independent extra total, never in an inferred
 output or reasoning category. Missing category values still use the shared
 numeric report shape; they do not establish a measured zero.
 
-Forked session files may replay the usage history of their parent. For Pi's
-tree-format sessions, the parent candidate follows the root-to-leaf path ending
-at the final physical entry rather than physical JSONL order; abandoned sibling
-and disconnected-root branches stay counted in the parent. The candidate includes
-only raw records at or before the child fork timestamp. The loader removes only a
-leading prefix that matches that candidate,
-and only when the parent file was discovered in the same store. Matching
-includes the timestamp, model, all token fields, the effective total-token
-fallback, and the effective billed cost in Display or Auto mode. The first
-mismatch and all later records remain in the child session. Missing, malformed,
-self-referential, or cyclic lineage is left unchanged so usage is not discarded
-speculatively.
+The local identity candidate accepts version 2 and 3 session trees with source
+session and entry IDs. Session names and projects come from the header, not the
+file location. An absent project stays unknown. Copies with the same session ID
+count once, even after a rename. Distinct entry IDs keep equal-sized calls.
+
+An explicit `parentSession` link must resolve to a selected file in the same
+store. The loader checks all recorded branches. Copied entries keep their source
+session; new child entries stay in the child. Pi can remove label records and
+change `parentId` during a fork, so cross-session comparison excludes that link
+field. Other source fields must agree. Short IDs in unrelated sessions stay
+separate. Time and token counts alone never prove a copy.
+
+Missing IDs, unsupported versions, conflicting source fields, invalid trees,
+missing parents, and malformed records fail the scan without a partial report.
+Legacy version 1 and headerless transcripts are unsupported by this candidate.
+A parent path never authorizes a read outside the selected files. Directory read
+errors and concurrent writes still need a separate completeness review.
 
